Not in this repository, but in images built from it
---------------------------------------------------

RP2040 second-stage bootloader
  A 256-byte precompiled blob, carried as data in the alloy-devices database
  (chips/raspberrypi/rp2040.yaml, `boot.license`) and emitted verbatim into the
  image for RP2040 targets.
  Licence   BSD-3-Clause — pico-sdk boot_stage2 (boot2_w25q080), taken
            precompiled and checksummed via rp-rs/rp2040-boot2.

Toolchain runtime (libgcc, newlib, libstdc++)
  Every image links parts of the cross toolchain's runtime. Which parts is a
  property of the build, not of this repository, so it is reported per image by
  `alloy sbom` from the linker's own map file. libgcc and libstdc++ are
  GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1; newlib is a collection of
  permissive licences whose text ships with the toolchain (alloy points at the
  path rather than asserting a single identifier).

alloy-devices
  The device database is a separate MIT-licensed repository. The register, pin
  and clock facts it holds are emitted into every generated source file.
